",", "lp": -0.008136080577969551, "top": [[",", -0.008136080577969551], [" (", -4.90047025680542]]}], "text": "Here's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part rebuild series of the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D, Intel Arc A770 16GB), spanning 2026-09-26 to 2026-10-01 across two Claude contexts (Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5), tracking commits b10146 \u2192 b12321.\n\n- **Major technical work:** The session covered a PKGBUILD rework, a `LLAMA_SUBPROCESS` ABI compatibility trap (commit d37dd50bb), SYCL graph optimizations, a oneDNN A/B comparison, a oneAPI 2026.0 \u2192 2026.1 upgrade (with a DLE swap), a PR #63 benchmark review, and a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch (commit 4e7400c3a).\n\n- **Driver/kernel transition:** The Intel Arc A770 switched from the i915 driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc1) to the **xe** driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc5) between the two contexts\u2014handled by other sessions, not this one.\n\n- **Performance investigation:** A key focus was a \"12-vs-18 t/s decode\" performance question, plus 256-GRF kernel builds and perplexity A/B testing, with benchmark data stored in dated research directories.\n\n- **Structure:** The document is organized into 14 sections\u2014identity/scope,"}